==Battleground==
*1 [[Lord Gravey]] spawns as the boss after 6.67 seconds<sup>200f</sup>.
*2 [[Mr. Mole]]s spawn after 16.67 seconds<sup>500f</sup>, delay 0.07 seconds<sup>2f</sup>.
*Infinite [[Znache]]s spawn after 23.33 seconds<sup>700f</sup>, delay 26.67~33.33 seconds<sup>800f~1,000f</sup>.
*Infinite [[Zroco]]s spawn after 20 seconds<sup>600f</sup>, delay 23.33~30 seconds<sup>700f~900f</sup>.
*4 [[Kang Roo]]s spawn after 40 seconds<sup>1,200f</sup>, delay 53.33 seconds<sup>1,600f</sup>.

==Strategy==
This stage can be somewhat difficult, as the constant knockback from the Mr. Mole will cause Lord Gravey's pushing power to increase exponentially. Because of this, you will want to use Wave attackers to quickly kill the Mr. Moles and Lord Gravey—such as [[Slime Cat (Rare Cat)|Jellycat/Jelly Dumpling Cat]] or [[Crazed Gross Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Manic Macho Legs]]. It is also recommended to use Long Distance attackers that can snipe the Mr. Moles, using Lord Gravey as a stepping stone.

== Trivia==
*The name of this stage references Jules Verne's novel [[wikipedia:Twenty Thousand Leagues Under the Seas|Twenty Thousand Leagues Under the Seas]]. The novel primarily explores the adventures of Captain Nemo and his submarine, the Nautilus. At the end of the book, Nemo decides to ask his crew to leave the submarine and flood it so he can be buried in it, thus making the Nautilus his tomb.

